1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,533
Some rivers in Japan still have

2
00:00:01,533 --> 00:00:02,518
warning signs.

3
00:00:02,531 --> 00:00:03,587
Not for floods.

4
00:00:03,796 --> 00:00:04,701
For the kappa.

5
00:00:05,213 --> 00:00:06,618
In Japanese folklore,

6
00:00:06,618 --> 00:00:08,034
the kappa is a river creature

7
00:00:08,034 --> 00:00:09,323
the size of a child,

8
00:00:09,323 --> 00:00:10,518
with a turtle shell,

9
00:00:10,530 --> 00:00:11,424
webbed hands,

10
00:00:11,424 --> 00:00:12,816
and a beak for a mouth.

11
00:00:13,026 --> 00:00:14,954
It hides in rivers and ponds,

12
00:00:14,954 --> 00:00:16,591
and drags horses and people into

13
00:00:16,591 --> 00:00:17,345
the water.

14
00:00:17,856 --> 00:00:19,283
But here's the strangest part.

15
00:00:19,714 --> 00:00:20,678
On top of its head is

16
00:00:20,678 --> 00:00:21,780
a dish of water.

17
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:23,881
That water is its power.

18
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:24,962
If it spills,

19
00:00:24,962 --> 00:00:26,319
the kappa grows weak.

20
00:00:26,947 --> 00:00:28,420
So how do you beat one?

21
00:00:28,758 --> 00:00:29,558
You bow.

22
00:00:29,989 --> 00:00:31,046
A kappa is polite,

23
00:00:31,046 --> 00:00:31,986
so it bows back,

24
00:00:31,986 --> 00:00:33,378
and the water pours out.

25
00:00:33,542 --> 00:00:35,214
Or you offer it a cucumber,

26
00:00:35,214 --> 00:00:36,362
its favorite food.

27
00:00:36,793 --> 00:00:38,463
The real animal behind it?

28
00:00:38,975 --> 00:00:41,425
One Edo-period naturalist probably drew his

29
00:00:41,425 --> 00:00:43,514
kappa from a softshell turtle.

30
00:00:44,026 --> 00:00:44,966
In some regions,

31
00:00:44,966 --> 00:00:46,789
the kappa even shares that turtle's

32
00:00:46,789 --> 00:00:47,426
name.

33
00:00:47,938 --> 00:00:49,760
So could a kappa actually work?

34
00:00:50,272 --> 00:00:51,513
Find out next.

